WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:05.192
This thing right here might as well be the
Loch Ness Monster with an iPhone 11,

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:09.690
or footage of an alien drinking a milkshake
in Area 51.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:14.294
It's a highly guarded secret, and anyone who
knows about it,

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:19.070
or has seen it, has been forbidden from
admitting that it exists for months.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:25.722
That is, of course, until it made its way
here to my kitchen counter, and now to you.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.726
Say hello to DJI's latest creation, the
RoboMaster S1.

00:00:35.813 --> 00:00:47.115
You all know DJI,

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.014
it's the world's largest drone maker,

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:52.840
and perhaps China's most popular tech
company.

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:57.925
People obsess over its products with an
Apple fanboy-like lust.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:03.233
And DJI delivers, bringing out one new drone
after another.

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:07.909
But now DJI has decided to bring its talents
to the ground.

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:08.393
With the RoboMaster S1,

00:01:08.765 --> 00:01:15.064
it has built a robot aimed at consumers who
want to drive around really fast,

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:18.446
and then shoot each other with pellets and
lasers.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:21.590
Because if there's one thing the world
really needed,

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:24.748
it's the violence of video games brought to
real life.

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:31.229
The idea for this new robot started here,

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:34.640
it's the annual RoboMasters competition

00:01:35.139 --> 00:01:36.983
that DJI holds in Shenzhen.

00:01:38.419 --> 00:01:40.865
College engineering students show up for a
couple of weeks

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:44.190
and try to destroy each other with a variety
of robots.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:47.750
As you can see, it's a lot of fun.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:51.716
The big idea then was to shrink these robots
down

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:54.490
to little ones, that regular people could
build

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.439
and then use in their own battles.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:03.430
You know what says "inspiration and
creativity live here"?

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.291
This poorly lit, brutalist building in the
Shenzhen suburbs

00:02:07.366 --> 00:02:10.707
that is a DJI research and development lab.

00:02:10.998 --> 00:02:16.091
Several months ago I came here to get a
firsthand look at prototypes

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.140
of the RoboMaster S1.

00:02:17.141 --> 00:02:23.347
This fellow here is the lead of the design
team

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.610
who helped bring this device to life.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.710
"Can you walk me through some of the
different parts?"

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:32.659
"So this is a video transmitter, and here is
a camera.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:36.111
And also there's a shooter mechanism."

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:38.783
"You've got the bullets in there?"

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.627
"Yeah, 90% of them are made of water.

00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:47.119
And when it hits things, it's smashed and it
disappears.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:51.666
And on each robot, the lights here indicates
the hit point.

00:02:51.756 --> 00:02:54.239
When you have repeated been hit,

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:57.649
the robot will end up being destroyed."

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:00.413
"That's the object of the game, is to chase
each other around

00:03:00.414 --> 00:03:01.443
and hit these plates?

00:03:01.535 --> 00:03:03.199
Is there like a laser?"

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:07.361
"Yeah, and if you always aim at the center
you should be fine."

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:08.970
"All right let's do it."

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:10.455
"Ok, let's do it."

00:03:28.833 --> 00:03:29.833
"Are you really good at this?

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:30.485
Are you just being nice to me?"

00:03:30.558 --> 00:03:33.946
"No no no. I'm a good driver, but not a good
shooter."

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:39.127
"So you've got the controller, but there's a
different mode

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.279
where you can just use your body?"

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.437
"In this way,

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:45.350
we allow people to control the movement of
the rover.

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:47.959
You can see it's a very sensitive."

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.932
Because DJI founder Frank Wang is a cruel,
cruel engineer,

00:04:01.788 --> 00:04:06.009
you cannot just buy a RoboMaster S1 and play
with it.

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:11.352
No, uou must first assemble it by hand

00:04:11.931 --> 00:04:15.727
and learn things along the way about
robotics and coding.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.650
Here's a group of youngsters DJI turned into
its product testing guinea pigs

00:04:22.768 --> 00:04:25.959
at something it billed as a summer camp.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.670
"This robot is also an educational tool to
teach programming language.

00:04:33.036 --> 00:04:37.570
For example, it can be used as a autonomous
driving car,

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.989
but we don't have built-in functionality for
this,

00:04:41.649 --> 00:04:46.579
kids have to learn to to program themselves
to achieve these functionalities."

00:04:47.529 --> 00:04:49.767
The hope is that this will teach kids a few
things,

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:51.478
get them hooked on robotics,

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:55.279
and turn into a worldwide sporting
phenomenon of sorts.

00:04:58.279 --> 00:05:02.431
"We hope that, in the future, robotics will
become a major sport,

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.237
like football, basketball.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:08.130
That's our vision for this product."

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:25.042
"Ow. I'm dead."  "Yes" "Nice game."

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:30.620
"My kids would die to play this."

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:36.910
And boys, daddy made your dream come true.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:40.610
Six months after my trip to China

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:43.676
I got my hands on a couple of the finalized
units.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:48.760
Here's my oldest son Bowie and his adorable
sidekick Tucker

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:54.130
who don't yet know just how bad the DJI
instructions are going to be.

00:05:54.759 --> 00:05:56.649
"Gentlemen, I have assembled you here today

00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:59.439
with cookies and milk for an important
project."

00:06:01.089 --> 00:06:02.979
"Are going to build a robot?"  "We are going
to build a robot, if you guys are up for
it."

00:06:04.662 --> 00:06:06.249
"You're going to have to do most of the
building."

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.751
Like a yak on about education and teachable
moments,

00:06:09.752 --> 00:06:14.760
but really I just wanted my kids to build
this thing so I could play with.

00:06:20.819 --> 00:06:22.413
"That's the coolest tool I've ever seen."

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:25.551
"Tucker look at this."

00:06:25.552 --> 00:06:26.140
"On your mark. Get set. Go!"

00:06:26.141 --> 00:06:32.126
It ships with this racing mode,

00:06:32.151 --> 00:06:35.499
where you can use computer vision to spot
targets placed around the house.

00:06:36.129 --> 00:06:37.068
"Engageing in close quarters."

00:06:37.069 --> 00:06:38.069
"Ow, I keep crashing."

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:44.590
Of course, what's more fun is shooting
pellets.

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:46.650
"Here's your orbs, boys."

00:06:51.169 --> 00:06:52.169
Or it has laser mode,

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:56.400
You know, for less mess.

00:06:57.569 --> 00:06:58.703
"This is the least fun part of the day."

00:06:58.704 --> 00:07:01.056
Will many people actually buy the RoboMaster
S1?

00:07:04.481 --> 00:07:07.272
It's hard to say.

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:11.160
The product requires a lot of actual work to
use.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:16.653
It's going to be expensive, and it's much
more nichey than DJI's usual devices.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:23.211
So it's fair to say the struggle is real for
DJI trying to create a global RoboMasters
army.

00:07:25.559 --> 00:07:30.600
As we see how things play out, let's just
hope that the kids remember to wear their
safety goggles,

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:34.470
and the DJI has a good insurance policy.

